# Spec-Kit Integration

Use the principles in `.specify/memory/constitution.md` for all development decisions.
When generating specs, plans, or tasks, refer to the templates in `.specify/templates/`.

## Available Slash Commands

When the user types any of the commands below, follow the instructions in the corresponding file exactly. Treat `$ARGUMENTS` as everything the user typed after the command name.

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `/speckit.constitution` | Define or update project guardrails and principles |
| `/speckit.specify` | Create a feature specification from a description |
| `/speckit.clarify` | Ask targeted clarification questions about the spec |
| `/speckit.plan` | Create a technical implementation plan |
| `/speckit.tasks` | Break the plan into dependency-ordered tasks |
| `/speckit.checklist` | Generate a requirements quality checklist |
| `/speckit.analyze` | Cross-artifact consistency and quality analysis |
| `/speckit.implement` | Execute implementation from the task list |
| `/speckit.taskstoissues` | Convert tasks into GitHub issues |

## Handoffs

Some commands offer handoff buttons (defined in their frontmatter under `handoffs`). When a command completes, present any handoffs as suggested next steps the user can take.

## Key References

- **Constitution**: `.specify/memory/constitution.md` (non-negotiable project principles)
- **Templates**: `.specify/templates/` (spec, plan, tasks, checklist, constitution templates)
- **Scripts**: `.specify/scripts/bash/` (setup, prerequisites, context update)
